{"problem": "top_n\n\nFind the k largest elements of a sequence\n\nOperates lazily in ``n*log(k)`` time\n\n>>> top_n(2, [1, 100, 10, 1000])\n(1000, 100)\n\nUse a key function to change sorted order\n\n>>> top_n(2, ['Alice', 'Bob', 'Charlie', 'Dan'], key=len)\n('Charlie', 'Alice')\n\nSee also:\n    heapq.nlargest", "resolution": "def top_n(k, seq, key=None):\n    \"\"\" Find the k largest elements of a sequence\n\n    Operates lazily in ``n*log(k)`` time\n\n    >>> top_n(2, [1, 100, 10, 1000])\n    (1000, 100)\n\n    Use a key function to change sorted order\n\n    >>> top_n(2, ['Alice', 'Bob', 'Charlie', 'Dan'], key=len)\n    ('Charlie', 'Alice')\n\n    See also:\n        heapq.nlargest\n    \"\"\"\n    if key is not None and not callable(key):\n        key = getter(key)\n    return tuple(heapq.nlargest(k, seq, key=key))\n", "text": "top_n"}